k  sections and then it has full page  illustrations so I kind of used that as  an inspiration to make the movie have a  hybrid quality and the idea was the 70s  underground comic book movement and  basing all of the drawings and the  animation because it's what many would  have been excited about and drawing on  are crumb and alien Kaminsky and GD  glitz and all of these really  interesting comic book artists that were  coming out of San Francisco at the time  so I wanted the in the animation to be  really tactile and feel hand-drawn it  was all drawn on paper I had one  animator who was really inspired by the  70s in her own work who hand drew every  frame of animation so it's hard to find  actually animators who do that kind of  animation these days and I just found  the perfect person and she and she took  the style of Phoebe's illustrations from  the book but she took them and ran with  them and she you know she filled her  notebook also she did all of the props  and all of the prop drawings and and  then hand her every frame of animation
 

